eoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root cause CONFIRMED by driven experiment (instrumented run_ensures under the recorded selection, then a 2s minimal pair):\n\nPOLLUTER: tests/unit/test_push_callers_best_effort.py:22 monkeypatches lock.canonical_tracker to a lambda returning its own tmp tracker, then calls event_append.write_and_push. event_append.py:350 lazily imports rebar._store.ensures for the FIRST time in the process; ensures.py:41 ('from rebar._store.lock import LockTimeout, canonical_tracker, write_lock') executed inside the patch window, permanently binding the test's lambda as ensures.canonical_tracker. monkeypatch teardown restores lock, not the captured copy.\n\nVICTIM: every later run_ensures (ensures.py:163) canonicalized ANY tracker to the polluter's dead tmpdir — instrumentation printed raw=<victim tracker> canonical=<.../test_event_and_batch_append_ke0/.tickets-tracker> realpath_fn=<...test_event_and_batch_append_keep_the_default_push_contract.<locals>.<lambda>>. The init-time sweep (gc-config pins gc.autoDetach/maintenance.autoDetach=false, .gitignore/.gitattributes/.ensure-applied) landed in the wrong dir while reporting changed; the victim tracker stayed UNPINNED, its 'git commit' spawned 'git maintenance run --auto --quiet --detach' (trace2 parent argv cited), and tests/_git_upkeep.py:203 correctly failed. The original 'origin gc threshold / trace scope' hypothesis is REJECTED: the fixture origin was pinned throughout; the detached child came from the tracker.\n\nRe-confirmed reproducing on origin/main aeab106820 (the spawn_detached/snapshot-GC merges c98d976199/7213e082b5/a3da2f4cce did NOT fix or move the mechanism). Minimal pair: test_push_callers_best_effort.py + the inline upkeep test (deterministic, 2.4s).\n\nFIX (class, not instance): ensures.py now late-binds via 'from rebar._store import lock as _lock' (the style event_append/sync/push already use; ensures was the only by-value importer of these names in src/rebar). RED->GREEN: new tests/unit/test_ensures_late_binding.py reproduces the patch-active first-import window and failed pre-fix, passes post-fix. Recorded 14-suite selection: 102 passed post-fix (2 runs). make lint, mypy, complexity ratchet (new=0 increased=0) green.","timestamp":1787352560493309001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RESOLVED — change landed. Gerrit change 2034 (Change-Id I59b5e18a0901409af4e6e983fd078b1c2579a8ff, 'ensures: late-bind lock.canonical_tracker') merged to main as 1496adf2b2 with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, no unresolved comments. Post-merge verification on origin/main tip 0b5356e741: tests/unit/test_ensures_late_binding.py (regression test pinning the patch-active first-import capture) + the minimal polluter/victim pair (tests/unit/test_push_callers_best_effort.py + tests/interfaces/store/test_inline_write_push.py) — 14 passed. Fix: ensures.py late-binds lock.canonical_tracker/write_lock/LockTimeout through the module object, removing the by-value import-capture class; adjusted tests/interfaces/store/test_ensures.py and tests/unit/test_ensures_boot_budget_e43f.py accordingly. Closing per acceptance criteria (all four boxes checked).","timestamp":1787356920479127001}],"created_at":1787338346763045001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"3f9fcb9c-9518-4081-9d5b-7121518ae0a1","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"3ff9-a8f0-ff5a-457f"},{"link_uuid":"d71f25dd-654f-47e4-b813-990f8aa52d5d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"672f-6966-40a4-49da"},{"link_uuid":"b3fdc7bf-7fc4-432c-a893-8db6ec34d79e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"71b0-5853-e9f8-4714"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\ntests/interfaces/store/test_inline_write_push.py::test_a_write_pushing_to_the_origin_leaves_no_detached_upkeep fails deterministically when run after tests/unit/test_push_callers_best_effort.py (minimal pair, 2s repro) and under the wider push-suite selection recorded earlier; it passes solo. Reproduced on origin/main a1a6a151bc and re-confirmed on aeab106820 (the spawn_detached/snapshot-GC merges did NOT fix it).\n\n## Root cause (confirmed by driven experiment)\n\nCross-module monkeypatch capture via a by-value import, aggravated by lazy first import:\n\n1. tests/unit/test_push_callers_best_effort.py:22 monkeypatches `lock.canonical_tracker` to a lambda returning ITS OWN tmp tracker.\n2. The test then calls `event_append.write_and_push(...)`; event_append.py:350 lazily imports `rebar._store.ensures` — the FIRST import of that module in the process.\n3. ensures.py:41 imports the function BY VALUE (`from rebar._store.lock import LockTimeout, canonical_tracker, write_lock`), executing while the patch is active, so `ensures.canonical_tracker` is permanently bound to the test's lambda. monkeypatch teardown restores `lock.canonical_tracker` but not the captured copy in `ensures`.\n4. Every later `run_ensures(tracker)` in the process (ensures.py:163) canonicalizes ANY tracker to the polluter's dead tmpdir: the whole init-time ensure sweep — including the `gc-config` unit's `gc.autoDetach=false` + `maintenance.autoDetach=false` pins and the .gitignore/.gitattributes/.ensure-applied writes — lands in the wrong directory while reporting `changed`.\n5. The victim test's freshly-inited tracker is therefore UNPINNED; its `git commit` (trace2: parent argv `git -C .../.tickets-tracker commit ...`) spawns `git maintenance run --auto --quiet --detach` at git's default autoDetach, and tests/_git_upkeep.py:203 correctly fails.\n\nRuntime evidence: instrumented run_ensures printed `raw=<victim tracker> canonical=<.../test_event_and_batch_append_ke0/.tickets-tracker> realpath_fn=<function test_event_and_batch_append_keep_the_default_push_contract.<locals>.<lambda>>`; the victim tracker post-init had no pins/no .ensure-applied while all units reported ok/changed. The fixture origin itself was correctly pinned throughout — the ticket's original \"origin past a gc threshold / trace scope\" hypothesis is rejected.\n\n## Approach\n\nFix the CLASS (import-time capture), not the one run: make `ensures.py` late-bind through the module object — `from rebar._store import lock as _lock` and call `_lock.canonical_tracker` / `_lock.write_lock` / `_lock.LockTimeout` at use time — exactly the style event_append.py, sync.py, push.py already use (ensures.py is the ONLY by-value importer of these names in src/rebar; nothing imports them FROM ensures). Behavior-preserving in production; removes the capture hazard for any patch-active first import. No change to the polluter test's contract (its monkeypatch is correctly scoped and now correctly confined).\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/_store/ensures.py (import + 6 call sites)\n- tests/unit/test_ensures_late_binding.py (new regression test)\n\n## Testing\n\nRED→GREEN regression test pinning the mechanism: pop `rebar._store.ensures` from sys.modules, import it while `lock.canonical_tracker` is monkeypatched to a decoy path, exit the patch, then assert `applied_ids(real_tracker)` reads the REAL tracker's `.ensure-applied` (old code: reads the decoy → fails RED). Test restores a clean ensures import in a finally so it cannot itself pollute. Plus: the minimal pair (test_push_callers_best_effort.py + the inline upkeep test) and the full recorded 14-suite selection pass deterministically; the upkeep oracle keeps its teeth (tests/_git_upkeep.py assertion unchanged — a genuinely unpinned remote still fails).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Root cause of the ordering-dependent detached upkeep is confirmed with a driven experiment (cited path:line evidence on the ticket).\n- [x] The recorded reproduction selection and the minimal pair pass deterministically after the fix.\n- [x] A regression test fails RED on the pre-fix import-capture mechanism and passes GREEN after.\n- [x] test_a_write_pushing_to_the_origin_leaves_no_detached_upkeep still fails RED when a push genuinely leaves detached upkeep (the oracle keeps its teeth).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/ensures.py","reason":"late-bind lock.canonical_tracker/write_lock/LockTimeout through the module to remove the by-value import-capture hazard"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ensures_late_binding.py","reason":"new RED->GREEN regression test pinning the patch-active first-import capture mechanism"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","672f-6966-40a4-49da"],["relates_to","71b0-5853-e9f8-4714"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"97facbb1-4cc6-4c94-a094-a3b9bae27121","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"d720-fc72-3763-4cac","ticket_type":"bug","title":"test_a_write_pushing_to_the_origin_leaves_no_detached_upkeep fails under a multi-suite push-test selection (ordering pollution)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6270125a-ecf4-4c20-b524-1baec61dde24","a4a3cb90-f87e-4d35-bfad-0aafeba48b7e","e64d9b2f-fcf4-48f2-8e7e-f429d3ba6410","8f13eaa8-bd9f-4174-af9c-e1d0e256ef6c","c7e3737a-22f9-4655-a28a-0ba0c261178f","ad3463f1-54ff-4456-bcfc-319cb78dad15","d71f25dd-654f-47e4-b813-990f8aa52d5d","b3fdc7bf-7fc4-432c-a893-8db6ec34d79e","44a3ac8c-90fc-4edc-b599-bcec4cb6067b","97facbb1-4cc6-4c94-a094-a3b9bae27121","87ce7089-521b-42bf-a66e-bac2218fb63f","0baabfbd-422b-46b2-be02-8a55a28a88cc"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787361446785731001,"uuid":"191b4b52-dbd6-4382-b03c-75611970fbc1"}